G-MP1|multi-pass-response-generation|~~closed=2026-03-14l~~
  what=Igor's output is single-pass LLM; feels "too automatic, too low level" (Akien flag)
  //
  // DESIGN DIRECTION (2026-03-14k session): build like the biology
  //
  // narrative_engine IS the TWM — not two things. TWM = current activation state of the graph.
  // NE = the process traversing that state, predicting what fires next. Predictions ARE activations.
  // Science: Global Workspace Theory (Baars/Dehaene) — TWM is the broadcast workspace;
  //          narrative is the competitive broadcast process; "conscious" response = pattern that won.
  //          Attractor dynamics (Hopfield/Grossberg) — loop terminates at stable state, not by step count.
  //          ART (Grossberg) — vigilance gate: match > threshold → resonate+commit; below → reject+search.
  //          Spreading activation (Collins/Loftus) — concurrent waves, not BFS; all at once.
  //
  // THE PROBLEM: no lateral inhibition. Highest-weight path wins immediately. No "too obvious" gate.
  // THE MECHANISM: gradient_flatness() on generation graph IS the vigilance signal.
  //   LOW flatness (close to 0) = STEEP gradient = strong dominant prediction = REFLEXIVE = inject warning
  //   HIGH flatness (close to 1) = FLAT gradient = no dominant prediction = novel OR graph-empty → D073 escalation
  //
  // IMPLEMENTATION (no extra LLM call — pure graph machinery):
  //   1. Before reply LLM call, run predict_next() on generation graph seeded by current context
  //   2. Compute gradient_flatness()
  //   3. If flatness > NPASS_FLATNESS_THRESHOLD → add to think context as:
  //      "[REFLEXIVE_PATTERN]: your generation graph predicts: {predicted_words}. If this feels too automatic, go deeper."
  //   4. Single LLM call uses or overrides the reflexive pattern — no second LLM call
  //   5. Gate: IGOR_NPASS_REPLY (already exists)
  //
  // WHY NO SECOND LLM CALL: inhibition happens BEFORE output (biology-correct), not after.
  //   The think context IS the workspace broadcast. Injecting the reflexive pattern + vigilance signal
  //   lets the LLM self-inhibit the obvious path. Cost: predict_next() + flatness() = microseconds.
  //
  // FILES: word_graph.py (LOW) — expose predict_next_with_flatness(seed_words) → (words, score)
  //        main.py (MEDIUM) — _build_think_context(): add generation graph prediction + REFLEXIVE_PATTERN
  //
  //
  // WHEN TO ESCALATE (D073): flatness() that NEVER converges (stays LOW after many cycles) = genuinely stumped.
  // Not "I don't know" as canned fallback. "I looked everywhere in the graph and I'm stuck."
  // Two signals from gradient_flatness():
  //   HIGH immediately → reflexive (D072: inhibit, re-traverse)
  //   NEVER converges → genuinely exhausted → THEN escalate to LLM
  // Factual queries: achievable soon. Fuzzy/generative: harder, deferred.
  // Book learning pipeline unchanged — that trains the graph; this changes when we query vs. escalate.
  //
  connects_to=G37p2 (IGOR_NPASS_REPLY + gradient_flatness() + generation graph all already built); D072; D073
  estimate=~2h; smaller than original framing; no new LLM calls; moves toward G11 (inference-free core)
  trigger=after IGOR_DUAL_WORD_GRAPHS enabled and has reply data to measure flatness against

  fix=PROC_GO_LEARN seeded; tools/learner.py wired; "go learn about X [tonight]" works end-to-end

